{"kind":"stack","id":"digestive-stack","title":"The digestive system","theme":{"background":"#fdf6e3","foreground":"#073642","font":"Arial, sans-serif"}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c1-term","content":"Mouth"},{"type":"text","id":"c1-expl","content":"The mouth breaks food into small pieces with the teeth and mixes it with saliva to start digestion."},{"type":"button","id":"c1-next","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c2","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c2-term","content":"Stomach"},{"type":"text","id":"c2-expl","content":"The stomach is a bag of muscle that churns food and mixes it with acid to break it down further."},{"type":"button","id":"c2-next","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c3","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c3-q","content":"Which part of the body breaks food into small pieces using the teeth?"},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a","label":"The mouth","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-b","label":"The liver","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-c","label":"The lungs","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c4-q","content":"Where does most of the digestion of food take place?"},{"type":"button","id":"c4-a","label":"The stomach","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-b","label":"The small intestine","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-c","label":"The bladder","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-d","label":"The windpipe","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c5-q","content":"What is the main job of the small intestine?"},{"type":"button","id":"c5-a","label":"To absorb nutrients into the blood","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-b","label":"To pump blood around the body","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-c","label":"To store air for breathing","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c6","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c6-q","content":"You eat a sandwich quickly and feel a lump in your throat. What do you do?"},{"type":"button","id":"c6-a","label":"Sit up straight and take small sips of water","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c6-b","label":"Lie flat on the sofa straight away","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c7","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c7-q","content":"Sitting up helps food move down the oesophagus into the stomach. The lump clears and you feel fine."},{"type":"button","id":"c7-next","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c8","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c8-q","content":"Lying flat makes it harder for food to travel down. The lump stays and you feel uncomfortable for a while."},{"type":"button","id":"c8-next","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c9","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c9-q","content":"Which organ stores bile, a liquid that helps break down fats?"},{"type":"button","id":"c9-a","label":"The gall bladder","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-b","label":"The kidney","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-c","label":"The spleen","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c10","kind":"end","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c10-h","content":"You finished the digestive system!"},{"type":"text","id":"c10-m","content":"Well done. You now know how the mouth, stomach and intestines work together to turn food into energy for your body."}],"actions":[]}}
